","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708059,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4MDU5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:2d","name":"topic:2d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":6,"created_at":"2026-09-04T14:55:24Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T15:44:47Z","closed_at":"2026-09-04T15:44:42Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot 4.7\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.stable - macOS Tahoe (26.5.2) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - AMD Radeon Pro 5300M OpenGL Engine - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-9750H CPU @ 2.60GHz (12 threads) - 16.00 GiB memory - CoreAudio (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn the PR https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/96188 the function `_update_cells()` was introduced as a way to fix the issue https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/96078 so that a `TileMapLayer` could emit a signal when cells are changed, for example\n\n```gdscript\n@tool\nextends TileMapLayer\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tchanged.connect(_on_changed)\n\t\nfunc _update_cells(_coords: Array[Vector2i], _forced_cleanup: bool) -> void:\n\tchanged.emit()\n\t\nfunc _on_changed() -> void:\n\tprint(\"TileMapLayer has changed\")\n```\n\nThis issue came up again in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107342 and `_update_cells()` was suggested but as mentioned by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107342#issuecomment-3369289759 if you are working with a terrain and paint, the call to `_update_cells()` deselects the terrain \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a `TileMapLayer` node with a script attached which implements `_update_cells`. Use the terrain paint feature and try and draw with the pencil. After one square, the `_update_cells` will deselect the terrain.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[tilemap-update-signal.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/31840427/tilemap-update-signal.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123193/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123193/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"not_planned","pinned_comment":null}